      "identification": "Go dating-app repository with editor-triggered JavaScript loader disguised as WOFF2",
      "verdict": "MALICIOUS",
      "evidence": [
        "Hidden folderOpen shell task launches public/fonts/fa-solid-500.woff2 with Node; workspace settings enable automatic tasks.",
        "The font is JavaScript with a 125-entry hex/XOR-0xf3 string table; rotation 54 resolves standard Node modules and Ethereum RPC method names.",
        "Queries recent blocks or sender transaction counts, with Blockscout transaction-list fallback, to select a configured sender transaction.",
        "decodeAddress reads the recipient as bytes and converts byte ranges [0,4) and [4,8) into IPv4 endpoints.",
        "HTTP GET, or HEAD header fallback, retrieves XOR-protected source. Source is evaluated and passed to detached node -e children with hidden windows."
      ],
      "limits": [
        "Final remote stages were not fetched; their effects are unknown.",
        "Activation depends on editor trust/task support and Node runtime module handling."
      ],
      "trait_changes": [
        "Move remote source activation from the legacy C2/dropper branch to execution/payload/script-eval.",
        "Add nested transaction-recipient read coverage.",
        "Move generic server-error and Go-template observations into neutral homes."
      ]
    },
    {
      "sha256": "a1ec081cb0d747f6f5d1d106d32b9ee38d108f6b9520b7145418e30b3d4f11e1",
      "identification": "PHP encrypted-request webshell",
      "verdict": "MALICIOUS",
      "evidence": [
        "The request field flows through Base32 decoding, an RC4 KSA/PRGA implementation with a fixed key, and PHP eval.",
        "The return value is encrypted with the same cipher and Base32 encoded for the response.",
        "Missing request field results in HTTP 404 and exit."
      ],
      "limits": [
        "No operator request or deployment context was supplied."
      ],
      "trait_changes": [
        "Existing two hostile request-execution/concealment traits are supported; no PHP-specific changes needed."
      ]
    },
    {
      "sha256": "1e10391637b3fb3e8e9d6de962f982f4b7398a8b51a7847619334974c841292e",
      "identification": "ADXPL-Forge 2.0.0 Active Directory audit and attack toolkit",
      "verdict": "BENIGN",
      "evidence": [
        "Wheel metadata explicitly advertises AD audit, credential, exploitation and emulation functionality.",
        "Console entry points lead to argparse and explicit module dispatch; import-time first-party code defines classes/functions/tables rather than launching an undisclosed payload.",
        "UAC and regsvr32/AppLocker modules print commands or generate payload text. The UAC module does not run registry commands.",
        "Other selected modules implement real operator-targeted LDAP/SMB/WinRM/SQL, credential-dump, ticket, spray and relay operations.",
        "Zerologon code attempts all-zero Netlogon authentication against the supplied target; it does not implement the password-reset operation its prose mentions.",
        "Ransomware/stealer emulation modules inspected are print-only stubs; the MITRE map is a reference catalog."
      ],
      "limits": [
        "No evidence of deployment authorization or operator intent was supplied.",
        "External dependencies, including xpl-core, were not included; this verdict concerns the supplied wheel."
      ],
      "trait_changes": [
        "Retain accurate offensive suspicious traits despite the BENIGN verdict.",
        "Replace hostile catalog and printed-UAC convictions with properly placed neutral facts and an execution-gated UAC composite.",
        "Remove unsupported RAT vocabulary, DLL-hijack and BITS-persistence aggregations; canonical operation detectors remain.",
        "Bind masquerading to a system-process filename within a temporary path.",
        "Treat imported libraries and referenced tool names as imports/references rather than the identity of the containing program."
      ]
    }
